cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TriAgent in your research, please cite the CIKM 2026 paper below."
type: software
title: "TriAgent: Divergence-Aware Multi-Agent Routing for Cost-Efficient LLM Inference"
abstract: >-
  TriAgent is a divergence-aware multi-agent routing framework that reduces
  large language model inference cost by routing each query to the cheapest
  model tier that can answer it correctly. It stratifies agents by contextual
  granularity (a word-level lexicon, a sentence-level domain transformer, and
  a cross-sentence LLM reasoner) and uses the Semantic Divergence Index (SDI),
  the pairwise disagreement between those tiers, as an unsupervised routing
  signal. The same SDI signal also serves as a multilingual semantic cache key
  and as a post-hoc LLM hallucination detector at AUC 0.90, with no additional
  model calls, labels, or training.
